<title>UK: Harding estate increases stake in Chelsea.</title>
<headline>Harding estate increases stake in Chelsea.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chelsea Village Plc, the holding company that owns Chelsea football club, said on Thursday that the estate of the late Matthew Harding had increased its interest in the company's shares to 27.34 percent.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that Harding's executors have exercised his option and have subscribed 4.5 million stg for 7.5 million new ordinary shares.</p>
<p>Harding was killed in a helicopter crash in October 1996.</p>
<p>At 0839 GMT, shares in the company were unchanged at 115p.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
